Scooters Scoreboard, LLC
ECEIVE
DEC 17 2024
To: Cheyenne City Governing Body
OFFICE OFCITYCLERK
From: Robert&Carla Winkler
7305 Ridge Road
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82009
This letter is inregards to requesting a l-year extension to theparked status of our liquor license
Wedevotedly owned and operated Scooters Bar from October 2015to2024.It became our
whole lives and we had good community support and a regular clientele.In 2023, we listed the
Scooters Bar building and barfor sale.We were getting older and thebar was taking an extreme
amount of our time andwe were ready to spend more timewith ourfamily and grandchildren.It
wasourhope that a buyer would come in and buy the entire operation and continue to run the
liquor store and bar so that we could retire.
Unfortunately, after much time and several failed offers, we were forced to sell our building
without theliquor license.Our books were still reflecting the hardknocks of COVID and the
liquor store and barwere deemed tooriskyfor mostbuyers.After our sale, were-grouped and
our intent was tomove to a smaller location and operate only theliquor store, not the bar.We
have searched for a building with good visibility and low cost tono avail.The cost of real estate
has risen.
We currently have our license listed with Teri Cassidyof #1Properties Commercial and are
currently in talks with a potential buyer.
Thank you,
Robert&Carla Winkler
